      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224403",
      ":question/problem": "An email server manager determined that $4%$ of the emails their clients receive are spam. After introducing a new filtering feature, the manager wants to know if the proportion of spam emails her clients receive has decreased. So, she decides to carry out a hypothesis test.\n\nLet $p$ represent the proportion of spam emails received after the filtering feature. State the null and alternative hypotheses for this test.\n\n$H_{0}$: {{field-1}}\n\n$H_{1}$: {{field-2}}"
