      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224404",
      ":question/problem": "A customer in a casino suspects that a roulette wheel numbered from $1$ to $36$ is biased toward landing on $9$. After alerting the croupier, they inspect the wheel and decide to carry out a hypothesis test.\n\nLet $p$ represent the probability that the roulette lands on $9$. State the null and alternative hypotheses for this test.\n\n$H_{0}$: {{field-1}}\n\n$H_{1}$: {{field-2}}"
